    "body": "claim released by issue-worker-high: no separate fix made. Open PR #817 (head 03437938, labelled `merge-ready`, not a draft) already carries the fix: its body ends `Fixes #824`.\n\n- **The fix in #817:** `march.rs` replaces the sphere trace (and its `phi == 0.0 => Read::Top(z)` arm) with a walk over cell centres. Each centre's sign comes from parity plus the cut claim, never from the stored magnitude. A centre on a stock plane reads by the half-open law: a centre on a floor plane is material, one on a top plane is air. The surface is then read from the bracket's ray-entry record or the shell crossing. If neither is on record, the read is `Unreadable`.\n- **Pinned by:** `a_stock_plane_on_a_cell_centre_reads_exactly_on_both_sides`. It covers this issue's own upright scenario (plate -6.25..0 on a 0.5 cell, slot to -6.0, expects `Material { top: -6.0, floor: -6.25 }`) and the flipped twin.\n- **Why no separate fix:** a fix on main would touch the same lines that #817 deletes. That would only add a conflict on #817 and leave code that gets thrown away. The issue closes when #817 merges, so it is labelled `in-review` against #817.\n",
